                                                      "label": "Paso 1: Regla de Oro ⭐",
                                                      "subject": "Diferencia entre Sustantivos Contables (se cuentan 1, 2, 3) e Incontables (líquidos, masas, granos).",
                                                      "formula": "[ Contables: an apple, three eggs ] vs [ Incontables: milk, cheese, bread, water ]",
                                                      "example": "We have two apples and an avocado (countables), but we also have some milk and rice (uncountables).",
                                                      "exampleEs": "Los incontables no tienen plural en inglés (no se dice 'milks' ni 'rices'); van con singular: 'The milk is fresh'.",
